                "evidence": "On the Pro plan, LatticeCache 2.3 costs **$45/month**, and the largest single item you can store is **5 MB**.\n\n**What the $45 includes each month:**\n- 20 GB of replicated NVMe cache storage\n- 50 million read ops\n- 10 million write ops\n\n**What you pay once you go over:**\n- Storage: $1.80 per extra GB-month\n- Reads: $0.12 per extra million ops\n- Writes: $0.60 per extra million ops\n\n**Other hard limits in 2.3:**\n- Maximum single item (value) size: **5 MB**\n- Maximum key length: 1,024 bytes\n- Maximum 2,000 concurrent client connections per cache namespace\n\nAs a worked example (my own arithmetic, not from the source): a month with 30 GB stored, 80M reads and 12M writes would cost $45 + (10 × $1.80) + (30 × $0.12) + (2 × $0.60) = **$67.80**.\n\n**Source:** the research vault page `wiki/LatticeCache.md`, which is based on LatticeCache's official pricing and limits page (updated 2026-11-02). The vault page was checked against that page on 2026-11-04 and was last reviewed 3 days ago. Pricing pages are re-checked every 30 days, so it's still current and I didn't search the web again.\n\nCoverage: vault searched and it answered everything; no web provider was used; no paid calls made."
